{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790438963748,"sessionID":"ses_f2187ab1cfferioCmfwlEPGWSC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_022d44f5ea2e43d49c315233","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore codebase structure","prompt":"Explore the codebase at /workspace thoroughly. I need to understand:\n1. The directory structure (key files and folders)\n2. The contents of res://data/units/unit_stats.gd\n3. The contents of res://scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd\n4. The contents of res://scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.tscn\n5. Any existing custom_nodes directory contents\n6. How Team enum is defined (look for it across the codebase)\n7. How BattleUnit is defined\n8. How UnitStats is structured\n\nReturn ALL file contents and directory listings in full. Be very thorough.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f21875b16ffewSXiawhmnEd7u3\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nHere is the complete and thorough exploration of the codebase at `/workspace`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Directory Structure\n\n```\n/workspace/\n├── .godot/\n│   ├── .gdignore\n│   ├── editor/\n│   │   ├── filesystem_cache10\n│   │   ├── main.tscn-folding-3ad5c15c4f3250da0cc7c1af1770d85f.cfg\n│   │   └── project_metadata.cfg\n│   ├── global_script_class_cache.cfg\n│   ├── scene_groups_cache.cfg\n│   └── uid_cache.bin\n├── data/\n│   ├── enemies/\n│   │   └── zombie.tres\n│   └── units/\n│       ├── bjorn.tres\n│       ├── unit_stats.gd\n│       └── unit_stats.gd.uid\n├── scenes/\n│   ├── battle_unit/\n│   │   ├── battle_unit.gd\n│   │   ├── battle_unit.gd.uid\n│   │   └── battle_unit.tscn\n│   └── main.tscn\n├── scripts/         (empty directory)\n├── project.godot\n└── task_config.json\n```\n\n**There is no `custom_nodes/` directory yet.** The `scripts/` directory exists but is empty.\n\n---\n\n## 2. `res://data/units/unit_stats.gd`\n\n**Full path:** `/workspace/data/units/unit_stats.gd`\n\n```gdscript\nclass_name UnitStats\nextends Resource\n\nenum Team {PLAYER, ENEMY}\n\nconst MAX_ATTACK_RANGE := 5\n\n@export var team: Team\n@export_range(1, MAX_ATTACK_RANGE) var attack_range: int = 1\n```\n\nKey details:\n- `UnitStats` extends `Resource`.\n- It defines **`enum Team {PLAYER, ENEMY}`** -- this is the only definition of `Team` in the entire codebase. `PLAYER = 0`, `ENEMY = 1`.\n- It exports `team` (typed to the `Team` enum) and `attack_range` (an int, clamped between 1 and `MAX_ATTACK_RANGE` which is 5, defaulting to 1).\n\n---\n\n## 3. `res://scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd`\n\n**Full path:** `/workspace/scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd`\n\n```gdscript\nclass_name BattleUnit\nextends Area2D\n\n@export var stats: UnitStats: set = _set_stats\n\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tif stats:\n\t\t_set_stats(stats)\n\n\nfunc _set_stats(value: UnitStats) -> void:\n\tstats = value\n\t\n\tif not stats or not is_node_ready():\n\t\treturn\n\t\n\tstats = value.duplicate()\n\tcollision_layer = stats.team + 1\n```\n\nKey details:\n- `BattleUnit` extends `Area2D`.\n- It has one exported property: `stats` of type `UnitStats`, with a custom setter `_set_stats`.\n- In `_ready()`, if `stats` is already assigned (e.g., by the scene/tres), it re-calls `_set_stats`.\n- In `_set_stats`, after duplicating the resource (to avoid sharing state), it sets the `collision_layer` to `stats.team + 1`:\n  - **Player** (team=0) -> collision_layer 1\n  - **Enemy** (team=1) -> collision_layer 2\n- **Notable:** There is a subtle issue on line 18 -- `stats = value.duplicate()` assigns the duplicated resource, but if `is_node_ready()` is false (line 15), the duplicate is assigned anyway. It duplicates the parameter `value` rather than the already-stored `stats`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. `res://scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.tscn`\n\n**Full path:** `/workspace/scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.tscn`\n\n```\n[gd_scene load_steps=3 format=3]\n\n[ext_resource type=\"Script\" path=\"res://scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd\" id=\"1_battle_unit\"]\n[ext_resource type=\"Resource\" path=\"res://data/units/bjorn.tres\" id=\"2_stats\"]\n\n[sub_resource type=\"RectangleShape2D\" id=\"1_body_shape\"]\nsize = Vector2(24, 24)\n\n[node name=\"BattleUnit\" type=\"Area2D\"]\ncollision_mask = 0\nscript = ExtResource(\"1_battle_unit\")\nstats = ExtResource(\"2_stats\")\n\n[node name=\"CollisionShape2D\" type=\"CollisionShape2D\" parent=\".\"]\nshape = SubResource(\"1_body_shape\")\n```\n\nKey details:\n- The root node is an `Area2D` named \"BattleUnit\" with the battle_unit.gd script attached.\n- It pre-assigns `stats` to the `bjorn.tres` resource (the Player unit).\n- `collision_mask` is set to 0 (won't detect anything by default -- this gets overridden by the script? Actually no, the script only sets `collision_layer`, not `collision_mask`).\n- It has one child: a `CollisionShape2D` with a `RectangleShape2D` of size 24x24.\n- There are **no** `DetectRange` or `TargetFinder` nodes present yet.\n\n---\n\n## 5. `custom_nodes/` Directory\n\n**No `custom_nodes/` directory exists.** The task_config.json instructs creating one with `detect_range.gd` and `target_finder.gd`, but they have not been created yet. The `scripts/` directory exists but is empty.\n\n---\n\n## 6. How `Team` Enum Is Defined\n\nThe `Team` enum is defined in a single location:\n\n**File:** `/workspace/data/units/unit_stats.gd` (line 4)\n```gdscript\nenum Team {PLAYER, ENEMY}\n```\n\n- `PLAYER = 0`, `ENEMY = 1` (GDScript enum defaults).\n- It is defined **inside** the `UnitStats` class, so it is referenced as `UnitStats.Team` from other scripts.\n- In the `.tres` resource files, `team = 0` means PLAYER and `team = 1` means ENEMY.\n\nUsage in the codebase:\n- `bjorn.tres`: `team = 0` (PLAYER)\n- `zombie.tres`: `team = 1` (ENEMY)\n- `battle_unit.gd`: `collision_layer = stats.team + 1` -- uses the integer value directly.\n\n---\n\n## 7. How `BattleUnit` Is Defined\n\n**File:** `/workspace/scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd`\n\n```gdscript\nclass_name BattleUnit\nextends Area2D\n\n@export var stats: UnitStats: set = _set_stats\n\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tif stats:\n\t\t_set_stats(stats)\n\n\nfunc _set_stats(value: UnitStats) -> void:\n\tstats = value\n\t\n\tif not stats or not is_node_ready():\n\t\treturn\n\t\n\tstats = value.duplicate()\n\tcollision_layer = stats.team + 1\n```\n\nIt is also registered in Godot's global script class cache:\n```\n/.godot/global_script_class_cache.cfg:\n\"class\": &\"BattleUnit\"\n\"base\": &\"Area2D\"\n\"path\": \"res://scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd\"\n```\n\nIt is instantiated in `main.tscn` three times:\n1. **\"WorkerMech\"** (group: \"workers\") at position (0, 0) with `stats = bjorn.tres` (PLAYER)\n2. **\"SaboteurNear\"** (group: \"saboteurs\") at position (65, 0) with `stats = zombie.tres` (ENEMY)\n3. **\"SaboteurFar\"** (group: \"saboteurs\") at position (150, 0) with `stats = zombie.tres` (ENEMY)\n\n---\n\n## 8. How `UnitStats` Is Structured\n\n**File:** `/workspace/data/units/unit_stats.gd`\n\n```gdscript\nclass_name UnitStats\nextends Resource\n\nenum Team {PLAYER, ENEMY}\n\nconst MAX_ATTACK_RANGE := 5\n\n@export var team: Team\n@export_range(1, MAX_ATTACK_RANGE) var attack_range: int = 1\n```\n\nIt is registered in Godot's global script class cache:\n```\n/.godot/global_script_class_cache.cfg:\n\"class\": &\"UnitStats\"\n\"base\": &\"Resource\"\n\"path\": \"res://data/units/unit_stats.gd\"\n```\n\n**Two instances exist as `.tres` resource files:**\n\n**`bjorn.tres` (PLAYER unit):**\n```\n[gd_resource type=\"Resource\" script_class=\"UnitStats\" load_steps=2 format=3]\n[ext_resource type=\"Script\" path=\"res://data/units/unit_stats.gd\" id=\"1_unit_stats\"]\n[resource]\nscript = ExtResource(\"1_unit_stats\")\nteam = 0\nattack_range = 2\n```\n\n**`zombie.tres` (ENEMY unit):**\n```\n[gd_resource type=\"Resource\" script_class=\"UnitStats\" load_steps=2 format=3]\n[ext_resource type=\"Script\" path=\"res://data/units/unit_stats.gd\" id=\"1_unit_stats\"]\n[resource]\nscript = ExtResource(\"1_unit_stats\")\nteam = 1\nattack_range = 1\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Scene Groups\n\nFrom `/.godot/scene_groups_cache.cfg`:\n```\ngroups = [\"workers\", \"saboteurs\"]\n```\n- \"WorkerMech\" is in group \"workers\" (PLAYER team)\n- \"SaboteurNear\" and \"SaboteurFar\" are in group \"saboteurs\" (ENEMY team)\n\nThis confirms all files, all directory contents, and every relevant definition across the codebase.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f2187ab1cfferioCmfwlEPGWSC","sessionId":"ses_f21875b16ffewSXiawhmnEd7u3","model":{"modelID":"deepseek-v4-pro","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Explore codebase structure","time":{"start":1790438843629,"end":1790438963734}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_fd577fd6-3eaa-4047-9d3e-42fc640880d0"}},"id":"prt_0de78a4dc001QbTroul1h50Qna","sessionID":"ses_f2187ab1cfferioCmfwlEPGWSC","messageID":"msg_0de78571f001rMBZ5llkUY34Ap"}}
